# Registry: Fiction

Made on purpose, held as made. No entry stands here at the first writing
(2026-11-07): the one worked example in the phext is Paper 001's own, and
it stands in Unknown on the say-so of the paper, not here. This scroll
stands empty on purpose, so that the first scene of our own making is
marked as made from the day it lands.
# Registry: transitions and receipts

A standing changes only along an allowed step, and only with the receipt
the step names: Unknown to True (a checking receipt lands); Unknown to
False (a refutation receipt lands); True to False (a refutation receipt
lands; the claim is stepped down, its history kept); False to Unknown (a
receipt is itself found wanting); Fiction to Unknown (a made scene is
taken up as a real proposal); Unknown to Fiction (a claim is re-marked as
show). No step enters True without a checking receipt. Fiction never
steps straight to True. Every step is written here, with its receipt.

