Q16. [synthesis — about this tracker] The Novelty Index counts
  concepts but is blind to DISTANCE: Paper 005's NI (0.15) scored
  lower than Paper 004's (0.18) despite being a total domain break,
  because six small concepts weigh less than five connected ones.
  Should NI gain a connectivity term — e.g. the giving of weights new concepts by
  whether they link to any existing scroll — and would that have
  priced Paper 002 (axis-opening, connected) vs Paper 005
  (axis-opening, disconnected) correctly in opposite directions?
